cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Aramaic Root Atlas: A Cross-Corpus Triliteral Root Explorer"
abstract: >-
  A cross-corpus triliteral root explorer for Aramaic literature,
  indexing 5,666 roots across 47,358 verses and 685,848 words from
  six corpora spanning ~1,500 years: Peshitta NT, Peshitta OT,
  Biblical Aramaic (Daniel, Ezra), Targum Onkelos, Targum Jonathan,
  and the Hymns of Ephrem of Nisibis. Features cross-script root
  normalization, 1,604 cognate root entries (Hebrew and/or Arabic) plus 405 Greek
  NT parallels, root family visualization, KWIC concordance,
  diachronic analysis, collocations, semantic fields (15 domains),
  word parser, passage lexical profiles, parallel viewer, frequency
  heat maps, researcher annotations, BibTeX/Zotero/Chicago/MLA/APA/SBL
  citation export, guided tour, in-app video walkthrough, and an
  interactive Swagger UI API reference. Quadrilingual interface
  (EN/ES/HE/AR) with RTL support, full sidebar navigation, and
  dark mode.
